Package: harnessr
Title: Compose, Budget, Cache, Record and Check Model Calls
Version: 0.6.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Justin", "Chase", email = "jchase.msu@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Author: Justin Chase [aut, cre, cph]
Maintainer: Justin Chase <jchase.msu@gmail.com>
Description: A toolkit for composing calls to large language models and
    keeping them under control: spending limits checked before each request,
    a response cache keyed on everything that changes a reply, recordings that
    can be replayed offline, a structured trace of every call, and checks of
    what came back. On top of that core sits a document-reading layer that
    ingests files, segments them into chunks, reads them to answer a
    question, and screens, extracts from and synthesises across a corpus.
    Every stage is registry-based, so users can add their own extractors,
    cleaners, segmenters and readers without editing the package.
URL: https://github.com/elkronos/harnessr, https://elkronos.github.io/harnessr/
BugReports: https://github.com/elkronos/harnessr/issues
